commit 6734d2d666e0c2d9f3f977dba16199ed764835b7
Author: YueGuobin <yueguobin@outlook.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 20:07:14 2026 +0800

    feat: add auto_connect flag and disconnect endpoint for computes
    
    Computes can now be flagged auto_connect in the database. The controller
    connects to flagged computes in the background at startup (reusing the
    one-second delayed fire-and-forget mechanism), and enabling the flag via
    PUT /computes/{id} triggers a background connection without the request
    ever waiting for it. Disabling the flag does not drop an existing
    connection.
    
    Add POST /computes/{id}/disconnect to tear a compute down manually: the
    notification stream and HTTP session are closed and every reconnection
    path (retry backoff, notification stream reconnect, lazy connection in
    http_query) is blocked until connect() is called again or the controller
    restarts with auto_connect enabled. Disconnecting a compute used by an
    opened project is rejected with 409 unless force=true; forcing only
    drops the controller-side control channel, nodes keep running unmanaged.
    The local compute cannot be disconnected.
    
    Also make test_compute_list create its own compute (it relied on rows
    from earlier tests and failed under reordering), and stop scheduling the
    delayed add_compute connection during tests: the timer leaked real
    connection attempts into other tests' event loops.

